=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
Every element of the reported fault was verified and found healthy. Router16's OSPF process is running correctly: it holds Router ID 172.30.1.1, participates in OSPF Area 0 (Backbone) with two active interfaces, and maintains two Full adjacencies — one to mswitch0 (172.16.30.254, via the bond0/10.2.2.x link-aggregate) and one to router7 (192.168.10.1, via eth2/172.30.1.x). Its FIB contains correct OSPF-learned routes to Campus 2 (10.5.0.0/24 and 10.6.0.0/24) and all backbone segments, all pointing correctly through router7. mswitch0, router7, router17, and sshswitch all have consistent, complete OSPF routing tables with Full adjacencies; no router shows any missing prefix or convergence problem.

End-to-end data-plane testing was performed from multiple Campus 1 PCs. PC5 (172.16.10.5, VLAN 10) and PC12 (172.16.30.12, VLAN 30) successfully pinged every Campus 2 host and gateway tested: PC1 (10.5.0.1), PC3 (10.6.0.3), sshswitch VLAN 5 gateway (10.5.0.254), sshswitch VLAN 6 gateway (10.6.0.254), and all backbone nodes (8.8.8.254, 10.0.0.1, 192.168.10.1) — all with 0 % packet loss. The reverse path (PC3 → 172.16.10.5) also succeeds. The single observed ICMP "Destination Host Unreachable" response from 55.5.1.2 when pinging 10.6.0.1 is not a network fault: 10.6.0.1 is simply an unassigned address in the VLAN 6 subnet (the actual hosts start at 10.6.0.3), so sshswitch correctly returns unreachable after an ARP miss.

Root cause: There is no fault. The helpdesk ticket is based on a false premise — the network is fully operational and the reported symptoms cannot be reproduced. No corrective action is required.
=== END ===